<SECTION image-layout="right" background-color="#1A1A1A">
  <IMG class="accent-image" query="Industrial green hydrogen production facility with massive electrolyzers and renewable energy infrastructure, dramatic lighting showing scale of clean energy transition">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Green Hydrogen Production Scales from Pilot Projects to Industrial Reality</SPAN></H1>
    <P><I><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Global green hydrogen production capacity expanded from 0.3 GW in 2023 to 2.1 GW in 2024, with committed projects reaching 8.7 GW by 2025. This seven-fold increase reflects electrolyzer cost reductions and renewable energy price declines that make green hydrogen competitive with gray hydrogen in industrial applications.</SPAN></I></P>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"><B>Production economics improved dramatically</B> as electrolyzer costs fell 35% annually and renewable electricity prices hit record lows. The Hydrogen Council reports green hydrogen production costs averaging <SPAN text-color="#00D4AA">$3.20/kg</SPAN> in 2024, down from $5.80/kg in 2022. Leading projects in Chile, Australia, and the Middle East achieve <SPAN text-color="#00D4AA">$2.50/kg costs</SPAN> with dedicated solar and wind installations.</SPAN></P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <SMART-LAYOUT variant="stats" cellSize="12">
          <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="0.3 GW">
            <P><B><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">2023 deployment:</SPAN></B> <SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">47 commercial projects, $5.80/kg average cost</SPAN></P>
          </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
          <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="2.1 GW">
            <P><B><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">2024 deployment:</SPAN></B> <SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">156 commercial projects, $3.20/kg average cost</SPAN></P>
          </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
          <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="8.7 GW">
            <P><B><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">2025 projected:</SPAN></B> <SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">340+ commercial projects, $2.40/kg target cost</SPAN></P>
          </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        </SMART-LAYOUT>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
    <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Industrial offtakers including steel, ammonia, and refining companies signed <SPAN text-color="#00D4AA">67%</SPAN> of green hydrogen production under long-term contracts, providing revenue certainty that enables project financing at scale.</SPAN></P>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>